[THOUGHT] The pain is localized to the medial tibia just below the patella — an atypical location for classic intra-articular pathology (e.g., meniscus tear, gout) and more suggestive of periarticular or bony origin. Key considerations now include:  
- Medial tibial stress syndrome (“shin splints”) — but usually bilateral and activity-related;  
- Tibial plateau or medial tibial condyle bone bruise or stress reaction — especially if weight-bearing or recent activity change;  
- Referred pain (e.g., from lumbar radiculopathy or hip pathology);  
- Less likely: tumor or infection (but no systemic signs, so lower priority).  
To narrow this, I need to assess functional impact (weight-bearing ability), mechanical features (locking, catching, giving way), and neurologic symptoms (numbness, tingling, radiation) to rule out nerve involvement or referred pain.

[QUERY] Can you bear weight on the affected leg? Also, do you feel any numbness, tingling, or pain radiating down the leg or up into the hip or back?

